WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Proof Case 007 — Summit Ridge Physical Therapy. One combined sentence on production.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:20.000
"I need a professional landing page for Summit Ridge Physical Therapy,
a boutique physiotherapy studio in Vancouver — services, team, and an online intake form.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:28.000
And automate it: when someone submits the intake form, email me the details
and add each lead to a Google Sheet."

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:36.000
One ask. The front person hires its team and the ticker shows the work in flight.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.500
After about three minutes.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:50.000
The landing page is live at a public address — preview ready, customer delivered —
while the build lane is still running.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Summit Ridge Physical Therapy: services, team, and the intake form on the live page.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.500
Same session. No second ask.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:14.000
The automation lane fires on its own and hands over a verified workflow file in Files.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Page plus workflow from one sentence. Edited live session — waiting is not shown in real time.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:26.000
The run receipt is on the Evidence Lab. The workflow is for import;
this film does not show it executing inside the client's n8n.
